---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Uses - Amirdaraee">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <div class="text-center mb-8">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/amirdaraee-setup.webp" type="image/webp">
        <img
          src="/amirdaraee-setup.jpg"
          class="max-w-full h-auto rounded-lg mx-auto"
          style="max-width: 60%;"
          alt="Amirhossein Daraee's development workspace featuring dual monitors, MacBook Pro, and ergonomic desk setup"
        />
      </picture>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">💻 Development Setup</h3>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Editors:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          I split my time between VS Code and JetBrains Rider — Rider for larger .NET projects and VS Code for everything else.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Theme & Font:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          It's Dracula everywhere. I've tried others, but nothing feels as balanced for long coding sessions.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Terminal:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          I use iTerm with oh-my-posh, because clean prompts and colorful segments make the command line feel alive.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">🧰 Tools & Apps</h3>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Productivity & Notes:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          I'm deeply into the Apple ecosystem, and Obsidian is my second brain. It's where I plan, journal, and map out project ideas.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Browser:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          I use Microsoft Edge everywhere — it's fast, integrated, and developer-friendly.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Extensions & Dev Tools:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          Nothing too fancy — I like to keep things minimal and distraction-free.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">🪑 Desk Setup</h3>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Main Gear:</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Monitor:</strong> LG UltraGear 27GR75Q-B (27", WQHD, HDR10, 165 Hz, 1 ms, 99% sRGB)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Keyboard:</strong> Logitech MX Keys
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Mouse:</strong> Logitech MX Master 3
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Computer:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          I currently use a MacBook M2 Pro with 16 GB RAM, and it's been an absolute powerhouse for development.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Ergonomics & Lighting:</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Desk:</strong> VASAGLE Height-Adjustable Electric Desk (120×60 cm, memory presets)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Chair:</strong> Dowinx Fabric Gaming Chair with spring cushion, headrest & footrest (grey)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Monitor Arm:</strong> HUANUO Gas Spring Mount (17–30")
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Light:</strong> Quntis Monitor Light Bar (touch control, anti-blue light, auto-dimming)
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">🧠 Workflow & Preferences</h3>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Languages & Frameworks:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          Mostly C#, Blazor, and TypeScript these days.
        </p>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Current Projects:</h4>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>🛒 Groceries price tracking app</li>
          <li>💥 Migraine tracking app (AuraTrack)</li>
          <li>⚙️ Smart file renamer CLI tool</li>
        </ul>

        <h4 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Can't Live Without:</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          Claude and Claude Code — they've become a natural part of my daily dev flow.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">🌐 Gadgets</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>🎧 Sony WH-1000XM4 (for deep focus)</li>
          <li>🎧 AirPods Pro 2 (for mobility)</li>
          <li>📱 iPad (for reading, sketching, and note-taking)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
